    [
      "heading",
      1,
      "virtualization",
      [
        [
          "text",
          "Virtualization"
        ]
      ]
    ],
    [
      "block",
      "paragraph",
      [
        [
          "text",
          "MiniOS can run as a guest in VirtualBox, VMware, QEMU/KVM, and Hyper-V."
        ],
        [
          "text",
          "\n"
        ],
        [
          "text",
          "Toolbox and Ultra also include software for running QEMU/KVM virtual machines from MiniOS itself."
        ]
      ]
    ],
    [
      "block",
      "paragraph",
      [
        [
          "text",
          "This page documents MiniOS-specific virtualization behavior. For ordinary VM creation and hypervisor settings, use the documentation of the hypervisor."
        ]
      ]
    ],
    [
      "heading",
      2,
      "running-minios-as-a-guest",
      [
        [
          "text",
          "Running MiniOS as a guest"
        ]
      ]
    ],
    [
      "heading",
      3,
      "recommended-vm-layout",
      [
        [
          "text",
          "Recommended VM layout"
        ]
      ]
    ],
    [
      "block",
      "paragraph",
      [
        [
          "text",
          "For the widest compatibility, attach the MiniOS boot media and any virtual disk that will contain a MiniOS live installation through an "
        ],
        [
          "span",
          "strong",
          [
            [
              "text",
              "IDE or SATA controller"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "text",
          ". This recommendation applies to VirtualBox, VMware, QEMU/KVM, and Hyper-V whenever such a controller is available."
        ]
      ]
    ],
    [
      "block",
      "paragraph",
      [
        [
          "text",
          "Other virtual storage controllers can work, but MiniOS must be able to access its live source during the initramfs stage, before the full kernel module tree from "
        ],
        [
          "span",
          "code",
          [
            [
              "text",
              "01-kernel-*.sb"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "text",
          " is available."
        ]
      ]
    ],
    [
      "heading",
      3,
      "early-boot-storage-support",
      [
        [
          "text",
          "Early-boot storage support"
        ]
      ]
    ],
